WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.203
- You talked about, you
know, all the misinformation.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.371
It's funny too.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.305
'Cause this is the
other thing I take away

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.673
from Jen Psaki's comment.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.109
They're the ones
identifying misinformation.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.344
Well, how many times have
they been wrong on that?

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.846
Over the last 40,

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.115
they told us the protesters
were peaceful last summer.

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:17.350
They told us that Republicans
defunded the police.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.852
They told us the
dossier was real.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.387
They told us Trump
colluded with Russia.

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:23.990
Bob Mueller did a $30 million
investigation and said,

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.025
that's not accurate.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.427
(soft music)

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.233
- I'm Dave Rubin.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.501
And joining me today
is a Congressman

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.603
for Ohio's fourth district.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:39.973
He serves as the ranking
member of the house judiciary

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:44.044
committee and is a co-founder
of the house freedom caucus,

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.011
Congressman Jim Jordan.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.279
Welcome to the Rubin Report.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.714
- It is good to
be with you, Dave,

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.482
and thank you for what you do.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.917
Thank you for
fighting for freedom

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:53.286
and first amendment liberties
for our, for everyone.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.188
And we, I mean, the
country appreciates that.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.689
So good to be with you.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.657
- Oh, well.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.692
I appreciate the kind words.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.927
I can bounce that
right back at you.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.162
You were one of the leaders,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.164
especially I think on
the big tech stuff,

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.699
fighting for free speech
and free expression

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.835
and keeping the
government and big tech

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.603
out of every little
facet of our lives.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.906
So actually let's,
let's start right there.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.107
- Sure.
- Big tech.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.442
Well, I'll give you the
broad question first

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.077
and then we'll get
into the specifics.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.812
Big tech, what do we do?

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.413
Do you want to regulate?

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.382
Do you want to break them up?

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.250
Do you believe
competition is enough?

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.819
Is it all of those?

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.087
Is it none of those?

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.322
- No. It's all of those
and probably some more.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.857
I mean, I do think
you've got to get rid

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:33.293
of the liability protection,
the so-called section 230.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.395
That's a start.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.529
Then I think you have to give,

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.598
and we have a series of,

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.233
there'll be in bill form soon.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.969
But ideas we're talking
about give her to 230,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.170
private right of action.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.072
Like big tech makes
some moderate,

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.540
content moderation
decision about you.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.842
They got to tell you why,

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:49.676
and there needs to
be some training.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.643
Why did they do that?

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:51.845
And frankly, if they do it

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.346
and like the DeSantis
did in Florida,

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.148
if you're a candidate for
office and they do those kinds

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.916
of things, there should
be a right of action,

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.985
you have to hold
them accountable.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.720
So that's something
we're looking at.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.155
And then frankly,

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.090
I think, you know, justice
Thomas has, I think,

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.927
more than hinted that he
wants to address this issue

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.530
and talking about big tech
and the power they have.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.633
So what we're also looking
at doing is speeding up

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:16.302
the antitrust actions
in our court system.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.172
So it gets to the Supreme
court and we can get an answer.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.274
After all the Trump
administration,

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:24.978
both the FTC brought antitrust
action against Facebook and

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.212
the justice
department has brought

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.381
an antitrust action
against Google.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.151
And we'll see how that all
shakes out with the Biden DOJ.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.520
But I think that's where
it has to focus versus

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.922
what the Democrats are
talking about doing,

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:39.659
which is just giving
more power to the FTC,

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.029
which I think would translate
into big government colluding

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:47.700
with big tech to further
stick it to conservatives.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.303
- Right, which is pretty much
what's happening already.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.272
On the 230 point.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:54.908
My audience is all they all
know about the difference

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.876
between platform and
publisher and all that.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:59.312
The pushback on
getting rid of 230,

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.080
which I'm basically
for getting rid of it.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.016
So I think we're pretty
much lined up there.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.217
The pushback though,

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.653
is that if you get
rid of the protections

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.788
that basically all
of these platforms,

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.223
Twitter, YouTube,
Facebook, et cetera,

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.992
that they will have to sensor
more because they'll be

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.427
worried about the liability.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.296
What would you say to that?

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.664
- Legitimate concern.

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.399
There's also the
concern that, you know,

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:22.835
they're so big, they
can handle the lawsuits

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.671
that come when they
do censor people

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:27.540
and versus the competition
that we want to have happen.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.077
But I just think the fundamental
issue is, look, if they're,

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.514
if they're making publishing
decisions, editorial decisions,

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.816
they're not supposed to have
the liability protection.

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.952
And that's, we know that
that's what they're doing.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.887
So I think you just
have to look at the,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.422
sort of the fundamental
question, say, okay,

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.057
you're making those
editorial decisions.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:47.660
you don't get the protection
and then go from there.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.329
But that's why I think you
also need the other things

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:52.365
I talked about to
actually address this.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.034
Again, what concerns me most is

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.703
in an effort to deal
with censorship.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:59.439
We have, we have people
embracing this idea that, oh,

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.175
we got to give the
government, the bureaucracy,

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.277
the agencies more
regulatory power.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.545
And I just think that's a mess.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:06.679
And frankly, we just saw this.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.081
We just saw this with Jen Psaki,

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.683
the spokesperson for the
president of the United States.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.985
I mean, think about
what she said.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.087
She said, big tech

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:16.222
are now where so many
people get their news,

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.624
ie they're the press.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.125
And so she said,

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:22.228
we are working with the press
to stop certain information

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.364
from getting to we, the
people, the American people.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:27.634
That is a direct violation of
their first amendment freedom

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.236
of the press liberties we have.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.504
That's scary.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.872
And they got some
list of 12 people

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.407
who they say are putting
out misinformation.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.342
So there's that sort of
fundamental question.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.011
I think that's, what's,
what the concern

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:41.614
is that marriage of big
government and big tech,

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:45.251
I think only means
conservatives, get it worse.

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:48.321
- When you hear Psaki say
something like that, her actual,

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.123
the word that to me was the,

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.458
where the real bell
went off was she said,

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:56.129
we flagged content for Facebook.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.498
The implication is we're
doing it together, right.

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:00.967
We're flagging it for them.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.201
When you hear that,

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.371
do you ever go to your
democratic counterparts

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:08.708
and go guys, look, we may
not agree on tax rates,

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.444
we may not agree on abortion
or blah, blah, blah.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:14.447
But I thought we at least
agreed on first amendment stuff.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.049
Do they, do they
take that meeting?

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.617
Do they take that call?

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.819
- They used to, I don't
know if they would now.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:22.922
And frankly, I have my, I'm
skeptical they would now.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:26.092
Because it has gotten
so, so partisan.

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.560
And we've had a
number of Democrats,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.295
some of them on the
judiciary committee,

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:30.863
the committee that's
supposed to safeguard

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.565
the bill of rights,
the constitution,

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.667
and American's fundamental
rights and liberties.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.670
We've had so many of
them cheer on big tech

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.205
when they sensor conservative.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.740
So it's not the same.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.409
It used to be that
you could work with.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:46.145
I mean, I always make
this, tell this story.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.681
Dennis Kucinich former
member is a friend of mine.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:49.916
I mean, I talked to him
on the phone a few months.

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:51.150
I just texted him yesterday

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.553
'cause I saw him on a,
on a clip on Tucker.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:56.022
Dennis is an old school
liberal who says,

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.024
let's make the best
arguments, have the debate.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.226
And he was with us
on civil liberties.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.928
But that's not where
today's left is.

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:03.663
Today's left is authoritarian

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:06.099
and you're seeing it
from the spokesperson

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:08.167
of the president of
the United States,

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.069
in the white house
briefing room.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:12.372
So it's a different
animal today.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:13.973
And again, I think that's
why you're so concerned

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.441
and I'm so concerned,

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.043
and so many Americans are
about what's really happening

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.077
to our freedoms.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.379
- Yeah. You know Dennis Kucinich

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:20.713
is actually a perfect example.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:21.948
When he ran for president,

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:24.016
which was, you know,
probably 16 years ago,

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.284
something like that.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:28.588
He was the furthest left
Democrat at that point.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:31.090
And basically the only people
who will talk to him now

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.825
are Tucker and Fox News.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.094
They would never put him
on CNN at this point.

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.896
- And he was a
champion of civil.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.232
We were on the oversight
committee together

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.234
when Democrats had power back,

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.903
when Dennis was in Congress.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.938
He chaired this subcommittee
I was the ranking mem.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:48.207
And when it flipped, I was
chairman, he was ranking member.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:49.909
And there were issues where
we could work together.

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:50.977
Typically they were civil.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.612
And like, we were both concerned

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:54.147
about facial
recognition technology

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:56.949
and how law enforcement might
use that to violate our.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.418
So we could work together.

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:00.753
And when we didn't agree,
he was a true liberal,

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.455
like let's have the
debate, let's have the.

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:04.257
Get your best hold and
make your best argument.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.792
Let's see who wins
after it's over,

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:07.894
we'll shake hands and we'll
get ready for the next issue

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:09.095
and have the debate.

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:11.030
That is so different
from what we see today,

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.832
where it's so the,

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.968
the vitriol and going after
people and the canceling

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.236
and everything else.

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.771
It is a completely
different animal.

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:20.940
I long for the,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.475
for the people like like
Kucinich, like Dennis Kucinich,

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.143
who's a good man,

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:26.512
and believes in so many
of the same things we do

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:28.181
when it comes to
civil liberties.

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.482
Different on policy,

00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:31.617
we're miles apart on
other policy issues.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.986
But, you know, we need
more of that, frankly,

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:35.288
in the United States, Congress.

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:36.789
- I think I've
asked this question

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.658
to every Congressman or
Senator that I've had on,

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:39.892
and I'd love to
know your take too.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:42.495
Do you know when,
do you have a moment

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:44.897
or was there a person
that you can point to

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:47.033
when the Democrats really
went off the deep end

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.501
with this stuff?

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:51.170
When it was okay, no more
talking, no more negotiating.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.573
You guys are all
bad guys, Nazis,

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:55.107
whatever nonsense
they're throwing at you.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.709
Do you remember
when it happened?

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.845
- Well, I mean,

00:07:58.845 --> 00:08:02.348
I would probably point
to November 8th, 2016,

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:03.649
when Donald Trump got
elected president.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:07.153
Because we know what
president Trump,

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.055
an individual by the
way who I think was,

00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:10.590
did an amazing job as president.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.892
Did more, of what he
said than any president,

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:14.227
certainly in my lifetime.

00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:17.763
Accomplished so much
with relentless attacks

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.132
from the left and the
Democrats and the media,

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.801
and frankly, too
many Republicans,

00:08:21.801 --> 00:08:23.769
and still got so much done.

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:24.971
But I think it
probably started then.

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:26.272
Now there may be something else.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:28.140
But the first thing
that popped to mind was

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.644
the day he wins election
Democrats have been, you know,

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:35.381
going after him and continue
to do so now five years later.

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:36.649
- Yeah. And then of course,

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.084
there's that moment
when Rashida Tlaib,

00:08:38.084 --> 00:08:39.585
the night she got
sworn in saying

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:43.489
she was going to impeach the
guy, years ago, years ago.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.725
I think you have to have a
crime before the guilt, right?

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:46.559
- Right.
- If I'm not mistaken.

00:08:46.559 --> 00:08:48.027
I'm a simple guy.

00:08:48.027 --> 00:08:50.530
- Yeah. But then we also learn,
I mean, you think about it.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:52.965
We learned that
the FBI was spying

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:54.500
on a presidential campaign.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.836
Like that's not supposed to
happen in our great country.

00:08:56.836 --> 00:08:59.505
A major party's political
or presidential candidate,

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:00.940
their campaign
was being spied on

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.642
by the other parties'
justice department,

00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:03.476
ie the FBI Jim Comey.

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:05.611
I mean, that's scary.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:07.647
And, Joe, you talk
about, you know,

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:09.448
all the misinformation.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:10.616
It's funny too,

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:11.551
'cause this is the
other thing I take away

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.885
from, Jen Psaki's comment.

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:15.321
They're the ones
identifying mis-information.

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:17.557
Well, how many times have
they been wrong on that?

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:19.058
Over the last 40.

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:21.360
They told us the protestors
were peaceful last summer.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.596
They told us that Republicans
defunded the police.

00:09:23.596 --> 00:09:25.064
They told us the
dossier was real.

00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:26.632
They told us Trump
