00:18:40.986 --> 00:18:44.189
about not only you, but
just Republicans in general.

00:18:44.189 --> 00:18:46.558
You know, obviously a
bunch of racist homophobes

00:18:46.558 --> 00:18:48.060
and all that nonsense.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.695
And you know, this will
shift us to another topic.

00:18:49.695 --> 00:18:51.997
But you know, you're
passing bills.

00:18:51.997 --> 00:18:54.566
You guys were always passing
bills to restrict voting.

00:18:54.566 --> 00:18:55.934
And then you look
at the actual bill.

00:18:55.934 --> 00:18:58.036
Not that the, not that
the media ever does it.

00:18:58.036 --> 00:18:59.571
And you're like, oh,

00:18:59.571 --> 00:19:01.340
well it causes, you know,
voter ID, that seems okay.

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:04.543
And you know, a paper
trail that seems okay.

00:19:04.543 --> 00:19:06.845
Making sure we count
correctly, that seems okay.

00:19:06.845 --> 00:19:08.347
But how much of your
day is just dealing

00:19:08.347 --> 00:19:09.648
with that sort of nonsense?

00:19:09.648 --> 00:19:10.916
- A fair amount.

00:19:10.916 --> 00:19:13.752
I mean, you know, but
I tell my colleagues,

00:19:13.752 --> 00:19:15.287
I tell guys in
the freedom caucus

00:19:15.287 --> 00:19:17.856
and colleagues on the
judiciary committee.

00:19:17.856 --> 00:19:19.158
I tell them, look,

00:19:19.158 --> 00:19:20.792
if the press isn't
saying something bad,

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:22.294
the mainstream press.

00:19:22.294 --> 00:19:23.529
If the press isn't saying
something bad about you,

00:19:23.529 --> 00:19:24.429
you're not doing
anything any good.

00:19:24.429 --> 00:19:25.898
So just under,

00:19:25.898 --> 00:19:28.100
'cause some people come here
and they think like, oh,

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:32.604
they're not used to just
the relentless attack

00:19:32.604 --> 00:19:34.439
you're going to get if
you're making a difference.

00:19:34.439 --> 00:19:37.109
So it's a shock for some people.

00:19:37.109 --> 00:19:39.077
But my attitude is you
have to embrace it because

00:19:39.077 --> 00:19:40.579
that's just the way it is.

00:19:40.579 --> 00:19:43.081
And it's not fun,
it's not pleasant.

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:44.716
And you just pushed back
by telling the truth.

00:19:44.716 --> 00:19:46.251
I always tell people.

00:19:46.251 --> 00:19:50.189
I think we make this job as
being a member of Congress,

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:51.924
we make it way too complicated.

00:19:51.924 --> 00:19:53.158
What did you tell the
voters you were going to do

00:19:53.158 --> 00:19:54.493
when you ran?

00:19:54.493 --> 00:19:57.362
They elected you to
do that, go do it.

00:19:57.362 --> 00:19:58.897
Make the argument,
make the case,

00:19:58.897 --> 00:20:01.667
do it in as compelling and
articulate way as you can.

00:20:01.667 --> 00:20:03.168
But go do that
and if you do that

00:20:03.168 --> 00:20:04.703
and the press calls
you all kinds of names

00:20:04.703 --> 00:20:06.138
and you're like you said,

00:20:06.138 --> 00:20:08.707
your racist and were
terrible and evil and all.

00:20:08.707 --> 00:20:10.175
Okay, fine. We
gotta, it's not fun.

00:20:10.175 --> 00:20:11.643
But we got a live with it.

00:20:11.643 --> 00:20:12.911
Just keep pressing on
because you're doing what

00:20:12.911 --> 00:20:13.712
you told the voters
you're going to do.

00:20:13.712 --> 00:20:15.247
And what I find is

00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:17.516
when you go back home
voters appreciate it.

00:20:17.516 --> 00:20:19.284
Even if they disagree with
you every once in a while,

00:20:19.284 --> 00:20:20.986
they'll say, I just liked
the fact that you're fighting

00:20:20.986 --> 00:20:21.920
and you're doing what you said.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.155
I don't agree with all of it.

00:20:23.155 --> 00:20:24.389
I agree with most of
it, but keep fighting.

00:20:24.389 --> 00:20:26.358
And that's what we're
supposed to do, I think,

00:20:26.358 --> 00:20:27.893
as a member of Congress.

00:20:27.893 --> 00:20:30.929
- So what do you make of the
Republicans that I sort of,

00:20:30.929 --> 00:20:32.197
at this point, you know,

00:20:32.197 --> 00:20:34.032
I'm kind of new to
this side, right.

00:20:34.032 --> 00:20:36.401
So I maybe have
fresh eyes on this.

00:20:36.401 --> 00:20:38.503
But you know, when I see
a guy like Mitt Romney

00:20:38.503 --> 00:20:40.038
or someone like Liz Cheney,

00:20:40.038 --> 00:20:43.475
I call them pet Republicans
because they go on MSNBC,

00:20:43.475 --> 00:20:45.611
they get pat on the head,
like they're doing anything.

00:20:45.611 --> 00:20:47.879
And then in essence,
they're Democrats.

00:20:47.879 --> 00:20:50.249
Now that's fine if that's what
they believe at this point.

00:20:50.249 --> 00:20:53.252
But when you guys get behind
closed doors, like, are you,

00:20:53.252 --> 00:20:54.386
do you say to them, hey,

00:20:54.386 --> 00:20:56.221
is there any
conservative principle?

00:20:56.221 --> 00:20:58.657
Is there any piece of
the Republican party

00:20:58.657 --> 00:21:00.158
that you guys are
here to defend,

00:21:00.158 --> 00:21:02.794
or is it just so that they're
nice to you on cable news?

00:21:02.794 --> 00:21:04.696
- Yeah. I just,
I never get that.

00:21:04.696 --> 00:21:08.834
I never get why some people

00:21:08.834 --> 00:21:11.503
want to go be the
Republican who attacks

00:21:11.503 --> 00:21:12.771
all the other Republicans.

00:21:12.771 --> 00:21:14.239
I mean, once in a while

00:21:14.239 --> 00:21:15.474
you're going to have some
squabbles, I get that,

00:21:15.474 --> 00:21:16.875
that's just normal
course of business.

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:18.910
But there's some Republicans
who want to go on TV

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:20.846
and just attack Republicans.

00:21:20.846 --> 00:21:23.115
And of course, CNN will
love you for a day,

00:21:23.115 --> 00:21:25.651
love you for a minute,
love you for a second.

00:21:25.651 --> 00:21:27.819
But as soon as you're
not doing that,

00:21:27.819 --> 00:21:29.721
then they're going to turn
around and start attacking you.

00:21:29.721 --> 00:21:32.124
And I never get like,
don't you see that?

00:21:32.124 --> 00:21:34.092
Don't, haven't you figured
out that they just,

00:21:34.092 --> 00:21:36.728
it doesn't take a genius
to figure this out.

00:21:36.728 --> 00:21:38.430
But yet you have
some people who,

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:40.532
who think their job
is to be the darling

00:21:40.532 --> 00:21:44.169
of CNN and attack Republicans.
I just never understood it.

00:21:44.169 --> 00:21:45.137
- Yeah. So, all right.

00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:46.672
So one other thing on big tech,

00:21:46.672 --> 00:21:48.340
and then we'll move on to
some of the other stuff.

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:49.908
Are you worried at all,

00:21:49.908 --> 00:21:51.476
this is sort of an extension
of the black pill question.

00:21:51.476 --> 00:21:54.246
But just that this stuff has
become so big that no matter

00:21:54.246 --> 00:21:56.615
what you do, no matter
what you do at this point,

00:21:56.615 --> 00:21:58.550
that do you think it's
possible that the ship

00:21:58.550 --> 00:22:02.187
has just sailed and the
government cannot do anything?

00:22:02.187 --> 00:22:04.323
- Look I'm concerned,
I'm nervous.

00:22:04.323 --> 00:22:05.757
I mean, don't misunderstand.

00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:07.592
I think, I think
it just, you know,

00:22:07.592 --> 00:22:09.394
obviously with the
question you asked,

00:22:09.394 --> 00:22:11.730
you have that you share
that same concern.

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:13.131
But I mean,

00:22:13.131 --> 00:22:15.100
I always come back to
like, this is America,

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:16.668
we're Americans,
we get things done.

00:22:16.668 --> 00:22:19.304
We've solved problems. We've
tackled all kinds of obstacles.

00:22:19.304 --> 00:22:21.807
I mean, you know, there's a,

00:22:21.807 --> 00:22:23.608
there's some people who make
the case that, you know,

00:22:23.608 --> 00:22:28.413
it's just this tough, rugged
attitude is in our DNA.

00:22:28.413 --> 00:22:31.416
You know, you think about the
people who started this place.

00:22:31.416 --> 00:22:32.617
Over in Europe, they said,

00:22:32.617 --> 00:22:34.119
you gotta practice your
faith a certain way.

00:22:34.119 --> 00:22:36.054
And they said, no, we don't.

00:22:36.054 --> 00:22:37.589
We'll get on the ship,
we'll risk it all.

00:22:37.589 --> 00:22:39.024
We'll go to this place called
America and we're going to do

00:22:39.024 --> 00:22:40.425
it the way we think
we need to do it

00:22:40.425 --> 00:22:42.127
and the way the good
Lord wants us to do it.

00:22:42.127 --> 00:22:44.262
And they did it and
we've overcome everything

00:22:44.262 --> 00:22:45.464
and become the
greatest country ever.

00:22:45.464 --> 00:22:48.967
So I still feel like
there's a ton of people

00:22:48.967 --> 00:22:50.202
who think like you and I do.

00:22:50.202 --> 00:22:51.937
Who think like the
folks I get to represent

00:22:51.937 --> 00:22:53.572
back in the fourth
district of Ohio.

00:22:53.572 --> 00:22:54.840
Who are willing to say,

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:55.841
no, we're not going
to let it happen.

00:22:55.841 --> 00:22:57.342
We're going to fight.

00:22:57.342 --> 00:22:59.344
We're going to do what
it takes in the right way

00:22:59.344 --> 00:23:02.781
to prevail in the end
for freedom, for liberty,

00:23:02.781 --> 00:23:03.882
for free speech.

00:23:04.883 --> 00:23:06.251
So I guess I'm optimistic.

00:23:06.251 --> 00:23:08.453
And maybe it's just
because I'm, you know,

00:23:08.453 --> 00:23:11.523
like you I'm American,
and I love the way we,

00:23:11.523 --> 00:23:13.191
we conquer things
to get things done.

00:23:13.191 --> 00:23:15.494
- Well I always tell people
I'm a world weary optimist.

00:23:15.494 --> 00:23:16.728
Because I'm an optimist,

00:23:16.728 --> 00:23:18.063
I don't think I could
do this if I wasn't.

00:23:18.063 --> 00:23:19.765
How could you say what
you think for a living

00:23:19.765 --> 00:23:21.133
if you were an optimist.

00:23:21.133 --> 00:23:22.367
But I'm also a realist.

00:23:22.367 --> 00:23:24.136
So that, that gives you
a little world weary.

00:23:24.136 --> 00:23:25.937
But to that point,
though, if there,

00:23:25.937 --> 00:23:27.172
if there are enough of us

00:23:27.172 --> 00:23:29.040
or let's say there's
more of us than them.

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.009
What do we do about some
of this election stuff?

00:23:31.009 --> 00:23:32.244
Because it seems to me.

00:23:32.244 --> 00:23:33.712
I played a clip on
the show last week,

00:23:33.712 --> 00:23:37.749
which was a compilation
of Democrats in 2018,

00:23:37.749 --> 00:23:41.052
including Kamala and
Klobuchar. You probably saw it.

00:23:41.052 --> 00:23:42.487
- Oh yeah.

00:23:42.487 --> 00:23:45.090
- It's about 15 Democrats
talking about rigged elections,

00:23:45.090 --> 00:23:47.225
talking about voting
machines that don't work,

00:23:47.225 --> 00:23:48.693
talking about hacking.

00:23:48.693 --> 00:23:50.896
All of the stuff that
I'm pretty sure you and I

00:23:50.896 --> 00:23:53.665
could get blown up here on
YouTube, right this very moment

00:23:53.665 --> 00:23:55.667
for talking about if
we talk about it now.

00:23:55.667 --> 00:23:56.868
- Right, right.

00:23:56.868 --> 00:23:58.837
'Cause Dave, you
forgot only Democrats

00:23:58.837 --> 00:24:00.972
are allowed to object
to election results.

00:24:00.972 --> 00:24:02.140
We can't object.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:03.642
- I always have to
make a note about that.

00:24:03.642 --> 00:24:04.910
- We're not allowed to.

00:24:04.910 --> 00:24:07.179
I mean, you think
about the folks on

00:24:07.179 --> 00:24:09.681
this January 6th commission
on the Democrat side.

00:24:09.681 --> 00:24:11.616
Bennie Thompson objected
to the election results

00:24:11.616 --> 00:24:13.518
in 2001 when president Bush won.

00:24:13.518 --> 00:24:15.320
Jamie Raskin, the lead
impeachment manager,

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:17.289
and impeachment round two,

00:24:17.289 --> 00:24:20.292
he objected to Florida
and on January 6th, 2017.

00:24:20.292 --> 00:24:23.862
Jim McGovern, Jim McGovern
on the day we had this,

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:28.967
the second impeachment debate
on the floor on January 13th,

00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:31.870
he brought up the week
before January 6th.

00:24:31.870 --> 00:24:33.305
And he said,
Republicans objected

00:24:33.305 --> 00:24:34.806
to the will of the people
last week when they

00:24:34.806 --> 00:24:36.641
try to overturn the will of
people and they objected.

00:24:36.641 --> 00:24:38.877
So I got up to speak right
after that and I said, well,

00:24:38.877 --> 00:24:41.913
you know, I said, I
said the fine gentlemen,

00:24:41.913 --> 00:24:43.148
the chairman of
the rules committee

00:24:43.148 --> 00:24:44.950
from Massachusetts, Mr.
McGovern said that we,

00:24:44.950 --> 00:24:46.485
we try to overturn
the will of people.

00:24:46.485 --> 00:24:48.687
I said, but guess who was
the first person to object

00:24:48.687 --> 00:24:50.355
on January 6th, 2017?

00:24:50.355 --> 00:24:51.823
Guess who was the first person?

00:24:51.823 --> 00:24:53.291
- I got an idea.

00:24:53.291 --> 00:24:55.227
- It was the right fine
gentleman from Massachusetts

00:24:55.227 --> 00:24:59.331
who objected to Alabama.
Think about that Dave.

00:24:59.331 --> 00:25:01.933
Alabama, president Trump
won by like 28 points.

00:25:01.933 --> 00:25:04.469
So he can object to Alabama,

00:25:04.469 --> 00:25:07.272
but Jim Jordan and Republicans
can't object to Pennsylvania

00:25:07.272 --> 00:25:09.674
where they unconstitutionally
changed their election law.

00:25:09.674 --> 00:25:11.109
I mean think about
this one fact.

00:25:11.109 --> 00:25:13.912
The election law passed
by the legislature,

00:25:13.912 --> 00:25:16.948
as the constitution requires
in Pennsylvania said

00:25:16.948 --> 00:25:18.683
election ends at
eight o'clock Tuesday.

00:25:18.683 --> 00:25:20.018
You know I mean of course,

00:25:20.018 --> 00:25:21.586
election day is
always on Tuesday.

00:25:21.586 --> 00:25:23.121
First Tuesday, after the
first Monday in November,

00:25:23.121 --> 00:25:24.556
it ends at eight
o'clock Tuesday.

00:25:24.556 --> 00:25:26.491
Democrats sued in the
partisan state Supreme court

00:25:26.491 --> 00:25:27.726
and the partisan
state Supreme court

00:25:27.726 --> 00:25:29.461
controlled by
Democrats says, nope,

00:25:29.461 --> 00:25:31.363
we don't care what
the legislature said.

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:32.631
We don't care what the law says.

00:25:32.631 --> 00:25:34.799
Election day now ends
at five o'clock Friday.

00:25:34.799 --> 00:25:36.668
They just extended the
election for three days.

00:25:36.668 --> 00:25:38.270
So I'm not allowed
to object to that.

00:25:38.270 --> 00:25:40.372
But Jim McGovern can
object to Alabama

00:25:40.372 --> 00:25:42.440
when Donald Trump wins
Alabama by 28 points.

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:43.608
You gotta be kidding me.

00:25:43.608 --> 00:25:46.011
So that's the part that drives.

00:25:46.011 --> 00:25:48.580
And it is my guess is you
spend a lot of your time doing

00:25:48.580 --> 00:25:50.048
the same thing I do,

00:25:50.048 --> 00:25:52.083
pointing out the freaking double
standard with these people.

00:25:52.083 --> 00:25:54.019
But you have to do
it because if not,

00:25:54.019 --> 00:25:55.520
they'll get away with it more.

00:25:55.520 --> 00:25:57.689
- Let's not forget. I think
his name is Josh Shapiro,

00:25:57.689 --> 00:25:59.424
the secretary of
state of Pennsylvania,

00:25:59.424 --> 00:26:01.526
who announced two days
before the election,

00:26:01.526 --> 00:26:03.962
that Biden was going
to win Pennsylvania

00:26:03.962 --> 00:26:05.530
before the election.

00:26:05.530 --> 00:26:07.599
- Yeah. The guy
counting the votes

00:26:07.599 --> 00:26:11.469
announces two days before
who's going to win.

00:26:11.469 --> 00:26:13.271
Maybe there's a problem with it.

00:26:13.271 --> 00:26:14.506
I mean call me crazy, call me.

00:26:14.506 --> 00:26:16.107
But they may be, there may be.

00:26:16.107 --> 00:26:17.175
You know, but of
course Democrats

00:26:17.175 --> 00:26:19.144
like all you guys are crazy.

00:26:19.144 --> 00:26:21.813
Somehow we're the conspiracy
theorist for just like,

00:26:21.813 --> 00:26:23.982
just like raising a
question about that.

00:26:23.982 --> 00:26:26.084
- So what do you guys
do on messaging them?

00:26:26.084 --> 00:26:27.352
Because I'm not kidding.

00:26:27.352 --> 00:26:28.920
I went through the
nine bullet points

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:30.522
in the last Texas bill,

00:26:30.522 --> 00:26:32.290
you know, on the
election that the HB3

00:26:32.290 --> 00:26:33.658
that they were going crazy over.

00:26:33.658 --> 00:26:34.492
And it really,

00:26:34.492 --> 00:26:36.161
it was things like ID.

00:26:36.161 --> 00:26:37.996
It was a paper trail.

00:26:37.996 --> 00:26:40.065
It was having cameras
when you're counting

00:26:40.065 --> 00:26:42.467
and a couple of very,
very basic things.

00:26:42.467 --> 00:26:44.369
There was nothing race in there.

00:26:44.369 --> 00:26:46.805
There was nothing to
stop anyone from voting.

00:26:46.805 --> 00:26:49.374
There were actually things like
actually extending benefits

00:26:49.374 --> 00:26:52.410
so employers could give more
time for people to vote.

00:26:52.410 --> 00:26:53.778
And yet it's called racist.

00:26:53.778 --> 00:26:55.947
It's repeated in
associated press

00:26:55.947 --> 00:26:57.215
and on NBC and everything else.

00:26:57.215 --> 00:26:59.818
Like how do you
beat that narrative?

00:27:01.219 --> 00:27:02.821
- You know, I think, well
again, you put out the facts,

00:27:02.821 --> 00:27:04.856
you do like, you
did. But I also...

00:27:04.856 --> 00:27:06.625
- Yeah, I'm past that point.

00:27:06.625 --> 00:27:08.360
What else do you
do besides that?

00:27:08.360 --> 00:27:09.961
- I think Americans get it.

00:27:09.961 --> 00:27:14.032
So take this, take this,
the Texas Democrats.

00:27:14.032 --> 00:27:15.567
So first of all,

00:27:15.567 --> 00:27:18.303
America sees Texas Democrats
getting on a private plane,

00:27:19.471 --> 00:27:21.172
you know, taking their
football and going home,

00:27:21.172 --> 00:27:22.907
not doing their
job, come into it.

00:27:22.907 --> 00:27:25.744
You know, this is emblematic
of what the Democrats think.

00:27:25.744 --> 00:27:27.212
I'm going to not do my job

00:27:27.212 --> 00:27:28.713
and I'm going to go to
Washington where I can say

00:27:28.713 --> 00:27:29.681
I'm a victim.

00:27:29.681 --> 00:27:31.549
That is like so Democrat, right.

00:27:31.549 --> 00:27:33.084
So they come to Washington,

00:27:33.084 --> 00:27:35.053
they spread COVID around
to everybody else.

00:27:35.053 --> 00:27:36.454
They found a plane with no mask.

00:27:36.454 --> 00:27:37.922
They probably had to show.

00:27:37.922 --> 00:27:40.625
So I think sometimes just
the common sense of Americans

00:27:40.625 --> 00:27:42.360
like these people are crazy.

00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:45.330
